  "question": {
    "text": "Four harmonic waves of equal frequencies and equal intensities <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> have phase angles <math><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math> . When they are superposed, the intensity of the resulting wave is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> . The value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let amplitude of individual wave is A<br >Then by using phasor method<br > <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image8-e8ca7198-dd34-45d2-9c44-f21b1fbdca50.jpg\"/> <br >So resultant amplitude <math><msubsup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow></mrow></math> <br > <math><mo>∴</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> <br > <math><mo>∴</mo><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
